question:
Imagine gaseous $\mathrm{Ar}$ at $298 \mathrm{~K}$ confined to move in a two-dimensional plane of area $1.00 \mathrm{~cm}^2$. What is the value of the translational partition function?
A. 3.9 x 10^{15}
B. 3.9 x 10^{17}
C. 3.9 x 10^{19}
D. 3.9 x 10^{21}

You are given the following reduction reactions and $E^{\circ}$ values:
\begin{align*}
\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}(a q)+\mathrm{e}^{-} \rightarrow \mathrm{Fe}^{2+}(a q) & E^{\circ}=+0.771 \mathrm{~V} \\
\mathrm{Fe}^{2+}(a q)+2 \mathrm{e}^{-} \rightarrow \mathrm{Fe}(s) & E^{\circ}=-0.447 \mathrm{~V}
\end{align*}
Calculate $E^{\circ}$ for the half-cell reaction $\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}(a q)+3 \mathrm{e}^{-} \rightarrow \mathrm{Fe}(s)$.
A. +0.324 V
B. -0.041 V
C. +0.041 V
D. -0.324 V
